# max-join-minimum: `MaxJoin` at its conformance minimum, 256, which every
# Core must honour exactly. `fan 257` starts one Join Member per pass, each a
# `call` record with the next call id. The first 256 start. Starting the
# 257th would pass the limit, so the Run faults at its `join-ask`
# (fanout:10, source 7:7) before the call reaches its Host function, and it
# gets no call id. The fault abandons the 256 pending members, one `abandon`
# record each in start order, after the `fault` record.
#
# The case doesn't answer 256 members to show a full Join completing: that
# the 256th member starts without a fault is what pins the minimum.
# Its Fuel, allocation and state figures are Cost Model 0's, as the TS Core
# blessed them.

